  "title": "About Pod Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "be5122a8320d633c",
      "text": "This plugin, type: **pod**, gathers pods of related wiki sites and adds them to your neighborhood. It augments the Present plugin: instead of only listing sister sites, you choose *which* pods to gather."
    },
    {
      "type": "pod",
      "id": "01b9d66d009aa2c7",
      "text": "POD"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "625ddc4e896c6e27",
      "text": "Write one **command** per line (UPPERCASE, an optional trailing colon \u2014 see the [[Fedwiki DSL Skill]] convention):\n\n- `POD` \u2014 `PARENT` and `SISTERS` together (shorthand)\n- `SISTERS` \u2014 sibling sites sharing the parent domain\n- `PARENT` \u2014 the parent-domain site itself\n- `CHILDREN` \u2014 direct sub-domains of this site\n- `DESCENDANTS` \u2014 all sub-domains, any depth\n- `FARM` \u2014 every wiki in the farm\n- `NEIGHBOURHOOD` \u2014 the sites currently in your neighborhood\n- `SNAPSHOT` \u2014 the current neighborhood *(same as NEIGHBOURHOOD)*\n\nAnd the **actions** (not site-kinds):\n\n- `ROSTER` \u2014 draw the gather compactly, mirroring a normal roster item\n- `TWIN` \u2014 only members that hold a page with **this page's slug**\n- `WATCH` \u2014 only members whose copy is *actually a fork* of it\n- `TITLE yes|no` \u2014 whether the `ROSTER` title shows (default yes)"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "4161c30927bd",
      "text": "### Mistyped commands\n\nA misspelled command is not silently swallowed. `CHIKDREN` names nothing, so the item would otherwise fall back to `SISTERS` and draw a pod nobody asked for. Instead the panel says *CHIKDREN \u2014 did you mean CHILDREN?* above the gather, in every display mode. A word that announces itself as a command \u2014 uppercase, the [[Fedwiki DSL Skill]] convention \u2014 but names none is always reported, even when no real command is close enough to guess. Ordinary lowercase prose stays data."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "7c1a4e0b9f2d5a86",
      "text": "### How it draws\n\nEvery pod is a **roster**: a heading, then the members' flags. Pod does not draw it \u2014 the [[Roster Plugin]] does, on every wiki there is, so pod builds the roster text and hands it over. The text it builds is exactly what the \u2744 icon saves as a page, so the drawn thing and the saved thing are one string.\n\nEach heading names the site the pod is relative to \u2014 *Sisters of fedwiki.club*, *The rest of the farm*, *Your neighbourhood*. `TITLE no` draws the flags with no headings at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "775aabdf4879ebab",
      "text": "### Retired commands\n\n`ROSTER`, `TWIN` and `WATCH` stay in the table rather than being deleted, because a word removed from the table is a word the parser reports as a mistake \u2014 and pages still say them. They parse, gather nothing, and say what became of them.\n\n`ROSTER` is the default now. `TWIN` and `WATCH` moved to the [[Twin Plugin]], which asks who holds *this page* rather than who is kin to *this site*."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "cedff82dadcf82fd",
      "text": "Each gathered site is registered as a neighbor, so its pages join your search and lineage. The page still reads normally without the plugin."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "9bebcef374d5",
      "text": "### Where a pod comes from\n\nThis plugin ships **no server**. It declares a specification and a module of plain functions, and the [[Farm Plugin]] mounts them \u2014 so the item reads its disk-derived pods from `/system/api/pod/roll.json`, the same address an agent uses. Kinship is arithmetic on names, and the only thing needing the disk is what sites exist: one directory read, no page counts.\n\n`NEIGHBOURHOOD` and `SNAPSHOT` ask nothing at all \u2014 they read the neighbourhood the browser has already assembled. Page counts and freshness come from each member's own sitemap.\n\nA wiki without the Farm Plugin says so in the panel instead of failing quietly; the requirement is declared in `fedwiki.requires`."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "c41e9b70a5d8362f",
      "text": "# Which Commands Cross\n\nA command language is a superset of an interface, never a mirror of one. Of the thirteen words below, five become a value of the `kinds` parameter and one is shorthand for two of those; the rest never leave the browser \u2014 `ROSTER` and `TITLE` because they are drawing choices the farm has no opinion about, and `NEIGHBOURHOOD`, `SNAPSHOT`, `TWIN` and `WATCH` because they read what only a browser holds. That last group is not a gap to be closed: no server could answer them however this plugin were written.\n\nThe table saying which is which lives in one module. The parser imports it and the plugin's interface declaration names it, so what an author may type and what the mounted operation accepts are one list read twice. See [[Pod API]] for the rendered version, and [[About Farm Plugin]] for how a declaration becomes a route."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "47fd6339cb39a685",
      "text": "## Repositories\n\n- **GitHub**: [Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-pod](https://github.com/Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-pod)\n- **npm**: [wiki-plugin-pod](https://www.npmjs.com/package/wiki-plugin-pod) \u2014 `npm install wiki-plugin-pod`"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "19d5c8a03e6b7412",
      "text": "# See\n\n[[Twin Plugin]] \u00b7 [[Roster Plugin]] \u00b7 [[Pod API]] \u00b7 [[Farm API]] \u00b7 [[About Farm Plugin]] \u00b7 [[Fedwiki DSL Skill]]"
    }
