    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "7c1a4e0b9f2d5a86",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "7c1a4e0b9f2d5a86",
        "text": "### TWIN and FORK \u2014 a roster of who else holds this page\n\nBoth turn the panel into a compact **roster of flags** (like a roster item): the matching members' flags flow inline, each linking to that member's copy of the page, the (sub)domain shown on hover. They differ only in strictness:\n\n- **`TWIN`** is **existence-only**, exactly like the wiki-client *Twins* strip \u2014 a slug match in the member's sitemap, read straight from the neighbourhood.\n- **`FORK`** is **lineage-aware** \u2014 it fetches each twin's page JSON and keeps only those whose journal carries a `fork` event. So a page that merely shares the name is a *twin*, not a *fork* (`FORK \u2286 TWIN`).\n\n```\nSISTERS\nFORK\n```"
      },
