        "id": "7c1a4e0b9f2d5a86",
        "text": "### ROSTER, TWIN and WATCH \u2014 compact rosters of flags\n\nAll three render like a **roster item**: the members' flags flow inline in the grey box, each linking to that member's copy of the page, the (sub)domain on hover. `ROSTER` shows the whole gather (mirroring a normal roster, with an optional left-aligned title toggled by `TITLE yes|no`); `TWIN`/`WATCH` filter it:\n\n- **`TWIN`** is **existence-only** \u2014 a slug match in the member's sitemap, like the wiki-client *Twins* strip.\n- **`WATCH`** is **lineage-aware** \u2014 it fetches each twin's page JSON and keeps only those whose journal carries a `fork` event (`WATCH \u2286 TWIN`): who is watching your page.\n\nThe `ROSTER` and table views carry a subtle **\u2744 icon** that saves the gather as a roster ghost page titled after the commands (e.g. `PARENT SISTERS Rosters`). No separate `FREEZE` command.\n\n```\nSISTERS\nWATCH\n```"
